Id: cron008f
Severity: FAIL
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Fix: chmod go-w the file, and read what it runs.
References: crontab(5), cron(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A file cron reads (/etc/crontab, a file in /etc/cron.d, a script in
/etc/cron.hourly, cron.daily, cron.weekly or cron.monthly, or a user's
crontab in the spool) can be written by anyone. Whoever writes to it
decides what cron runs next, and as whom: root, for every file but a
user's own crontab. Any account on the system can take root this way.

Take write permission away from everyone but the owner (chmod go-w), and
look at the file's contents and at who might already have changed it.
